# Authorization policies

## Plugin semantics

Policies encapsulate allow/deny decisions for resources and actions. Controllers request authorization through the plugin’s authorize APIs used by the project.

## Required behavior

- Create/update policies consistent with app naming and plugin docs for the installed version.
- Pass the correct resource (entity/query/class) for the check.
- Cover allow and deny cases in tests.
- Keep mass-assignment tight on entities involved in authorized updates.

## Anti-patterns

- Giant policies that mix unrelated resources
- Authorizing only in the browser/API client
